{"id": "EUVD-2026-103933", "enisaUuid": "b80c98a3-347d-3a3d-8828-398e887432e8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: accel: kxcjk-1013: reject duplicate event disable\n\nThe IIO core does not filter duplicate writes to the event enable\nattribute. kxcjk1013_write_event_config() already ignores repeated\nenable requests, but a repeated disable request still calls\nkxcjk1013_set_power_state(data, false), dropping a runtime PM reference\nthat was not acquired for this request. This can underflow the runtime\nPM usage count and trigger a \"Runtime PM usage count underflow\" warning.\n\nReturn early when the requested state already matches ev_enable_state.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:45:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:39", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/137c35cff4d4d69f73cbfc0bf7870bf379a7a364", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad690c0c1b9131725619e352cb7c970488cbf436", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3365209e758c845a197211645731f0e393a86012", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa94a37b5a3e560c277dac6f9e5d0d75549a6583", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd30c10ff60d2b30386c23bb7c61cc97f2385c97"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jg4r-9rqj-mgw5", "CVE-2026-98679"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "191d83c0-b2b1-328d-a885-b8f91f725630", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "1d553977-9063-3657-afdf-c5eff5a3e785", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b4b491c0832ef90a7a5070e5975bc8427f2049ca <aa94a37b5a3e560c277dac6f9e5d0d75549a6583"}, {"id": "5b3898f6-695b-37ff-b0ea-b8e59a14d88f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b4b491c0832ef90a7a5070e5975bc8427f2049ca <dd30c10ff60d2b30386c23bb7c61cc97f2385c97"}, {"id": "687c23c6-835f-3069-b007-647a4575a19d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_v